Step-by-Step Guide: Enabling PR QA Review on Other Repositories
Prerequisites
Before enabling the workflow on other repositories, ensure:

✅ Central automation repository is configured:

Repository: WeBuildAgents/engineering-automation
File: .github/workflows/reusable-pr-qa-review.yml (with --trust flag fix applied)
File: cursor/prompts/pr-review.md
Both committed to main branch


✅ Secrets are configured at organization or repository level:

CURSOR_API_KEY (required)
SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL (optional)


✅ GitHub CLI installed (for automated rollout):

bash   # Install gh CLI if needed
   brew install gh  # macOS
   # or visit https://cli.github.com/
   
   # Authenticate
   gh auth login

Option 1: Automated Mass Deployment (Recommended)
Use the rollout script to deploy to multiple repositories automatically.
Step 1: Configure the Rollout Script
Edit scripts/rollout-pr-qa-review.sh:
bash# Repositories to skip (will NOT receive the workflow)
SKIP_REPOS=(
  "engineering-automation"  # Skip the automation repo itself
  "private-repo"            # Add any repos you want to skip
)

# Optional: Only deploy to specific repos (leave empty to deploy to all)
ALLOWLIST_REPOS=(
  # "openclaw-global-skills"
  # "openclaw-vps-setup"
)
Step 2: Run the Rollout Script
bash# Clone the automation repository
git clone https://github.com/WeBuildAgents/engineering-automation.git
cd engineering-automation

# Make the script executable
chmod +x scripts/rollout-pr-qa-review.sh

# Run the rollout
./scripts/rollout-pr-qa-review.sh
Step 3: What the Script Does
The script will automatically:

✅ List all repositories in the WeBuildAgents organization
✅ Skip repositories in the SKIP_REPOS list
✅ Clone each repository
✅ Create a new branch: chore/add-pr-qa-review
✅ Add the workflow file: .github/workflows/pr-qa-review.yml
✅ Commit and push the changes
✅ Create a PR with description
✅ Move to the next repository

Step 4: Review and Merge PRs

Go to each repository in GitHub
Review the automatically created PR titled: "chore: add reusable PR QA review workflow"
Verify the workflow file looks correct
Merge the PR

Example PR created by script:
Title: chore: add reusable PR QA review workflow

Body:
## Summary
This PR adds the reusable PR QA review workflow wrapper.

## Changes
- adds `.github/workflows/pr-qa-review.yml`
- wires the repository to the centralized reusable workflow in `WeBuildAgents/engineering-automation`

## Notes
- review logic is centralized
- secrets are inherited from organization/repository configuration

Option 2: Manual Deployment (Individual Repositories)
Use this for enabling the workflow on a single repository manually.
Step 1: Navigate to Target Repository
bashcd /path/to/your/repository
# Example: cd ~/projects/openclaw-global-skills
Step 2: Create Workflow Branch
bashgit checkout main
git pull origin main
git checkout -b chore/add-pr-qa-review
Step 3: Create Workflow Directory
bashmkdir -p .github/workflows
Step 4: Create Workflow File
Create .github/workflows/pr-qa-review.yml with this content:
yamlname: PR QA Review

on:
  pull_request:
    types: [opened, synchronize, reopened]

# Some org/repo policies force `GITHUB_TOKEN` to `pull-requests: none` by
# default; declare permissions at BOTH the workflow and the job level so the
# reusable workflow inherits the scope it needs.
permissions:
  contents: read
  pull-requests: write

jobs:
  qa-review:
    permissions:
      contents: read
      pull-requests: write
    uses: WeBuildAgents/engineering-automation/.github/workflows/reusable-pr-qa-review.yml@main
    secrets: inherit
    with:
      slack_enabled: true
      slack_title: "PR QA Review"
      # Reusable workflow default is 400000; override only if you routinely
      # review PRs significantly larger than that.
      max_diff_chars: 400000
      fail_on_block: true
Step 5: Commit and Push
bashgit add .github/workflows/pr-qa-review.yml
git commit -m "chore: add reusable PR QA review workflow"
git push -u origin chore/add-pr-qa-review
Step 6: Create Pull Request
bash# Using GitHub CLI
gh pr create \
  --title "chore: add reusable PR QA review workflow" \
  --body "Adds automated PR QA review using centralized workflow from engineering-automation"

# Or manually create PR on GitHub web interface
Step 7: Merge the PR
Once reviewed, merge the PR to enable the workflow.

Verification Steps
After deploying (automated or manual), verify the workflow is working:
1. Create a Test PR
bash# In the target repository
git checkout -b test/verify-qa-review
echo "# Test change" >> README.md
git add README.md
git commit -m "test: verify QA review workflow"
git push -u origin test/verify-qa-review
2. Create PR on GitHub
bashgh pr create --title "test: verify QA review" --body "Testing automated review"
3. Check Workflow Execution

Go to the PR on GitHub
Navigate to "Checks" tab
Verify "qa-review / qa-review" appears
Wait for workflow to complete (~2-5 minutes)

4. Verify Review Comment

Check the PR "Conversation" tab
Verify a comment appears with:

✅ ## Summary
✅ ## Code Quality Report
✅ ## Missing Tests
✅ ## Coverage Risk
✅ ## Recommendations
✅ ## Recommendation (APPROVE/NEEDS TESTS/BLOCK)



5. Verify Slack Notification (if enabled)

Check your configured Slack channel
Verify message appears with:

Repository name
PR number
Final recommendation
Review summary



6. Verify Workflow Behavior

If recommendation is APPROVE: Workflow passes ✅
If recommendation is NEEDS TESTS: Workflow passes ✅ (warning only)
If recommendation is BLOCK: Workflow fails ❌ (prevents merge)


Configuration Options
You can customize the workflow per repository by editing .github/workflows/pr-qa-review.yml:
Disable Slack Notifications
yamlwith:
  slack_enabled: false  # ← Change to false
Allow Merge Even on BLOCK
yamlwith:
  fail_on_block: false  # ← Change to false (workflow will warn but not fail)
Adjust Diff Size Limit
yamlwith:
  max_diff_chars: 600000  # ← Increase for very large PRs (default: 400000)

Notes:
- Argv length is NOT the bottleneck — the diff is passed to cursor-agent via a
  file path inside a short driver prompt, so this cap is only about token spend
  and model focus, not Linux's MAX_ARG_STRLEN limit.
- When the diff is clipped the workflow appends an explicit marker
  (`[DIFF TRUNCATED]`) that instructs the reviewer agent to raise a HIGH-
  severity coverage finding instead of silently approving the tail.
Custom Slack Title
yamlwith:
  slack_title: "OpenClaw PR Review"  # ← Custom title

Troubleshooting
Issue: Workflow doesn't trigger
Solution:

Check .github/workflows/pr-qa-review.yml exists in main branch
Verify PR event types: [opened, synchronize, reopened]
Check GitHub Actions is enabled: Settings → Actions → General

Issue: "Unrecognized named-value: 'secrets'" error
Solution:

Ensure reusable-pr-qa-review.yml in engineering-automation has the Slack fix applied (removing secrets.SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL from if condition)

Issue: Review comment not posted
Solution:

Check workflow logs for errors
Verify pull-requests: write permission is granted
Ensure Cursor CLI installed successfully (check "Install Cursor CLI" step)

Issue: "Workspace Trust Required" error
Solution:

Ensure reusable-pr-qa-review.yml uses --trust flag:

python  ["cursor-agent", "--trust", "-p", full_prompt]
Issue: Missing CURSOR_API_KEY
Solution:

Go to organization settings: https://github.com/organizations/WeBuildAgents/settings/secrets/actions
Add CURSOR_API_KEY secret
Or add at repository level: Repository → Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions

Issue: Slack notification not sent
Solution:

Verify SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL secret exists
Check slack_enabled: true in workflow
Test webhook URL manually:

bash   curl -X POST -H 'Content-type: application/json' \
     --data '{"text":"Test message"}' \
     YOUR_SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL

